WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.980 --> 00:00:01.820
Welcome!

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:02.680
Thanks!

00:00:03.720 --> 00:00:05.180
You ...

00:00:05.540 --> 00:00:10.060
We saw some images of you when you were 15, now you're 16.

00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:14.420
From the climate conference in Poland.

00:00:15.140 --> 00:00:17.600
What was that like for you ...

00:00:17.600 --> 00:00:22.260
... to speak there and to be there? Was it impressive seeing ...

00:00:22.260 --> 00:00:25.880
... how this climate work happens, close by?

00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:31.020
It was definitely an incredible opportunity to be able to be there.

00:00:31.020 --> 00:00:32.780
Not a lot of people are allowed to be there.

00:00:32.780 --> 00:00:36.200
But it's quite depressing being there, because you think that ...

00:00:36.300 --> 00:00:41.860
Our future is in the hands of these people.

00:00:41.920 --> 00:00:44.800
And they don't seem to take that seriously.

00:00:44.800 --> 00:00:46.640
That makes you pretty scared.

00:00:46.680 --> 00:00:48.520
In what way?

00:00:48.520 --> 00:00:50.660
They are there, after all.

00:00:50.740 --> 00:00:53.740
Yes, but it feels like they ...

00:00:53.740 --> 00:00:55.760
They don't really want to be there, in a way.

00:00:55.760 --> 00:00:58.020
They're only there because it's a UN conference.

00:00:58.020 --> 00:00:59.880
It doesn't feel real.

00:00:59.880 --> 00:01:03.400
In the dining room, everyone eats hamburgers, for example, and that ...

00:01:06.520 --> 00:01:07.140
Okay?

00:01:07.380 --> 00:01:10.500
There's not a lot happening, it's mostly talk.

00:01:11.340 --> 00:01:14.680
You weren't more optimistic when you left than when you came?

00:01:14.680 --> 00:01:20.160
No, I wasn't. But it was still very cool to be able to speak in front of everyone, to ...

00:01:20.160 --> 00:01:23.000
... to have something to say and to have it said.

00:01:23.000 --> 00:01:23.500
You ...

00:01:29.580 --> 00:01:33.560
This has made a huge impression.

00:01:33.620 --> 00:01:37.200
But it's an involvement that ...

00:01:37.200 --> 00:01:39.460
... you've had a while now.

00:01:39.960 --> 00:01:41.820
Can you remember ...

00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:45.620
... how this involvement began with you?

00:01:46.620 --> 00:01:48.740
How it began?

00:01:49.020 --> 00:01:50.480
It was ...

00:01:50.800 --> 00:01:52.700
Some years ago, I might have been ...

00:01:52.700 --> 00:01:55.220
8 or 9 years old, I went to elementary school and ...

00:01:56.000 --> 00:02:00.960
And my teachers were talking about climate change, and hoe we should turn off the lights when we left the room, and ...

00:02:01.060 --> 00:02:03.280
... that we should save water.

00:02:03.440 --> 00:02:04.480
And things like that.

00:02:04.760 --> 00:02:10.360
And I remember one instance when we were watching a movie about plastic in the ocean.

00:02:10.960 --> 00:02:12.620
And climate change. And then ...

00:02:12.620 --> 00:02:14.600
We watched the movie, and then ...

00:02:14.600 --> 00:02:19.380
I cried through the movie, and the other children were of course also very affected.

00:02:20.680 --> 00:02:23.920
And when the movie was finished, the teacher immediately after said:

00:02:23.920 --> 00:02:27.440
«Next week you'll have a substitute teacher, because I'll be at a wedding in New York.»

00:02:27.660 --> 00:02:29.060
And I thought ...

00:02:29.580 --> 00:02:35.400
«They just said that airplanes was a cause, how can they say that and still ...»

00:02:35.780 --> 00:02:36.860
«... fly.»

00:02:36.860 --> 00:02:42.080
And I thought it was very strange that they could say one thing and do another, because I'm a person who ...

00:02:42.520 --> 00:02:45.880
... doesn't like saying one thing and doing another, so ...

00:02:46.340 --> 00:02:49.680
It sparked an interest in me, and I started reading.

00:02:49.680 --> 00:02:51.300
I borrowed books and ...

00:02:51.640 --> 00:02:54.340
Saw movies. Read articles. And ...

00:02:54.340 --> 00:02:57.180
The more you read, the more you understand.

00:02:57.320 --> 00:02:59.160
And when you understand ...

00:02:59.300 --> 00:03:02.700
... the climate crisis, you can't ...

00:03:02.820 --> 00:03:05.100
... escape, then you're stuck.

00:03:12.180 --> 00:03:14.020
Do you think that that is ...

00:03:14.760 --> 00:03:16.920
... part of the problem, that ...

00:03:17.140 --> 00:03:21.300
... a lot of people don't fully understand the climate crisis?

00:03:21.620 --> 00:03:25.360
Yes, absolutely. Most people don't understand ...

00:03:26.580 --> 00:03:31.060
Most people know that the planet is getting warmer because of greenhouse gasses.

00:03:31.060 --> 00:03:34.260
Caused by our emissions.

00:03:34.660 --> 00:03:37.220
And that that can lead to ...

00:03:37.520 --> 00:03:41.600
... ice melting, more extreme weather and it getting warmer.

00:03:41.740 --> 00:03:44.780
But they don't know the consequences of that.

00:03:44.780 --> 00:03:47.820
And how serious it actually is. And they don't know ...

00:03:47.820 --> 00:03:50.300
... what it takes to prevent it.

00:03:50.620 --> 00:03:54.060
You have been open about having Asperger's.

00:03:54.220 --> 00:03:59.160
In what way has that affected you in this case ...

00:03:59.160 --> 00:04:02.580
... would you say, when it comes to your climate interest?

00:04:02.580 --> 00:04:04.940
It think it has affected everything.

00:04:04.960 --> 00:04:06.360
Because if ...

00:04:06.760 --> 00:04:11.100
If I didn't have Asperger's and if I wasn't so strange, I would be stuck in this ...

00:04:11.100 --> 00:04:14.640
... social game that everyone else seems to be so infatuated with.

00:04:22.920 --> 00:04:23.760
But ...

00:04:24.700 --> 00:04:30.120
It makes me function a bit differently. I see the world in a different way, with a different perspective.

00:04:30.120 --> 00:04:33.440
And I think that if I didn't have this, then I wouldn't ...

00:04:33.780 --> 00:04:35.940
... have been able to see it from the outside.

00:04:35.940 --> 00:04:39.900
I see things very much as black and white.

00:04:39.900 --> 00:04:45.120
And most people say that: «It doesn't matter if I do a little of this. Nothing is black and white.»

00:04:45.120 --> 00:04:48.180
But the climate question is actually black and white.

00:04:48.280 --> 00:04:53.480
In one way, it's the most complicated question that exists, and it will take ...

00:04:53.560 --> 00:04:56.580
...a  huge effort to stop it.

00:04:56.580 --> 00:05:01.620
But the solution is still simple enough for a five-year-old to understand.

00:05:01.620 --> 00:05:03.860
We have to stop the emissions. It's black and white.

00:05:03.860 --> 00:05:06.520
Because either we will start a chain reaction ...

00:05:06.520 --> 00:05:10.880
... that triggers events that triggers events beyond human control ...

00:05:10.880 --> 00:05:12.320
Or we don't.

00:05:12.320 --> 00:05:13.880
Does that mean that you ...

00:05:13.880 --> 00:05:17.560
We have an expression in Norwegian that says «live what you teach».

00:05:17.680 --> 00:05:19.280
Do you do that yourself?

00:05:19.720 --> 00:05:20.720
Can you manage?

00:05:20.720 --> 00:05:22.780
Yes, I hope that I do. I have ...

00:05:23.240 --> 00:05:25.180
... stopped flying ...

00:05:25.180 --> 00:05:29.660
... become a vegan, and I have a «shopping stop», which means that I don't buy new things.

00:05:29.960 --> 00:05:31.080
And that ...

00:05:32.920 --> 00:05:38.480
That's a choice I've made because I can't stand up for these ...

00:05:38.940 --> 00:05:43.100
... causes without doing my part.

00:05:44.160 --> 00:05:46.540
If not I would have such a bad conscience.

00:05:46.980 --> 00:05:49.080
You have ...

00:05:50.020 --> 00:05:55.520
... two parents ... And your mother is a famous opera singer, Malena Ernman.

00:05:57.040 --> 00:06:01.120
Have they been affected, have they changed their lifestyle?

00:06:01.260 --> 00:06:03.840
Eh. Yes.

00:06:04.080 --> 00:06:08.880
I made my parents stop flying some years ago.

00:06:08.880 --> 00:06:12.020
And especially since my mother is dependent ...

00:06:12.200 --> 00:06:18.680
... or was dependent, on flying for work, she was forced to change her career, in some way.

00:06:19.220 --> 00:06:24.740
Because she's a very famous singer, with a big career?

00:06:25.400 --> 00:06:26.580
But ...

00:06:26.580 --> 00:06:29.220
That doesn't help, the excuse is too poor?

00:06:29.240 --> 00:06:32.520
Yes. She does musicals instead now, in Stockholm.

00:06:39.040 --> 00:06:41.900
Do they shop, then?

00:06:45.600 --> 00:06:48.360
Definitely not as much as they used to, but ...

00:06:48.420 --> 00:06:50.920
It does happen that they do.

00:06:51.740 --> 00:06:56.260
Do they then try to keep it hidden from you?

00:06:56.280 --> 00:06:57.140
To hide away ..?

00:06:57.140 --> 00:06:58.140
Yes.

00:06:59.520 --> 00:07:00.580
But I ...

00:07:00.580 --> 00:07:05.680
It's difficult to hide things from me, I can tell when people are lying.

00:07:05.940 --> 00:07:07.840
And then ...

00:07:07.840 --> 00:07:10.720
And then they have to tell me, and I will scold them.

00:07:11.440 --> 00:07:14.640
So you walk around the house like a sort of police?

00:07:14.640 --> 00:07:15.440
Mhm!

00:07:16.660 --> 00:07:19.120
And i go through their receipts!

00:07:20.920 --> 00:07:22.420
You do?!

00:07:23.180 --> 00:07:24.840
Sometimes, yes!

00:07:24.840 --> 00:07:26.200
You've said that ...

00:07:26.760 --> 00:07:31.160
... that this involvement with the climate has made you well.

00:07:31.260 --> 00:07:31.960
Mhm.

00:07:32.240 --> 00:07:34.080
In what way were you unwell?

00:07:35.360 --> 00:07:37.640
Some years ago ...

00:07:37.720 --> 00:07:41.100
I became depressed.

00:07:41.500 --> 00:07:43.780
I could only stay at home.

00:07:43.860 --> 00:07:46.100
I stopped going to school. And ...

00:07:46.340 --> 00:07:49.940
I stopped eating, stopped talking.

00:07:50.360 --> 00:07:53.340
Because I felt that there was no meaning with life.

00:07:53.380 --> 00:07:54.320
So then ...

00:07:54.320 --> 00:07:56.760
Why did this happen?

00:07:57.180 --> 00:08:01.900
I don't know. There were a number of reasons. But one reason was ...

00:08:02.160 --> 00:08:04.580
... climate change. And ...

00:08:04.580 --> 00:08:08.780
... what is happening to the environment and the climate. That ...

00:08:08.980 --> 00:08:11.860
It was happening, and no one cared. That ...

00:08:11.960 --> 00:08:15.000
Our society is so shallow. We only focus on ...

00:08:15.060 --> 00:08:18.220
... what's on the surface, instead of ...

00:08:18.520 --> 00:08:22.300
... what is happening on the inside. And ...

00:08:24.300 --> 00:08:29.880
Everything goes so fast. The hamster wheels turn faster and faster, and then ...

00:08:32.160 --> 00:08:36.740
I fell off these hamster wheels, in some way. And then ...

00:08:36.860 --> 00:08:40.700
And I saw it from the outside and thought: «This is wrong.»

00:08:40.700 --> 00:08:45.660
That we can't continue like this, because you don't end up anywhere on a hamster wheel.

00:08:46.100 --> 00:08:48.180
There's so much on the outside.

00:08:48.180 --> 00:08:54.200
And you feeling better, does that have to do with your involvement and that you've become more active..?

00:08:54.320 --> 00:08:55.120
Yes.

00:08:55.760 --> 00:08:57.760
Yes, absolutely. Because ...

00:08:58.320 --> 00:09:03.500
I realized in some way that there's so much to live for. There's so much ...

00:09:04.520 --> 00:09:07.080
One can try to improve the world and ...

00:09:07.080 --> 00:09:11.280
... make a difference. And I thought that I would try to do just that.

00:09:23.180 --> 00:09:27.260
You've received a huge amount of attention for this ...

00:09:27.260 --> 00:09:32.320
... not least because you started a school strike that has been copied all around the world.

00:09:32.320 --> 00:09:34.740
There are strikes all over the world.

00:09:34.740 --> 00:09:35.660
Yes.

00:09:36.980 --> 00:09:42.200
There have been strikes inn all continents except Antarctica!

00:09:42.420 --> 00:09:43.440
Which is ...

00:09:44.680 --> 00:09:45.520
I'm still waiting!

00:09:45.700 --> 00:09:48.280
The penguins are a little behind?

00:09:49.000 --> 00:09:51.540
Yes. They need to catch up!

00:09:51.540 --> 00:09:54.780
But it's very cool that it has spread out all over the world.

00:09:54.780 --> 00:09:57.500
Literally. There have been ...

00:09:57.560 --> 00:10:03.160
... tens of thousands of people, mainly young people, who have ...

00:10:03.800 --> 00:10:08.780
... gathered in front of parliaments or town halls.

00:10:08.780 --> 00:10:11.380
And you're still doing this.

00:10:11.400 --> 00:10:15.240
How long are you planning to sit there and keep doing this?

00:10:16.000 --> 00:10:19.280
Until Sweden is in line with the Paris agreement.

00:10:19.560 --> 00:10:21.980
And that can take a few years.

00:10:24.840 --> 00:10:25.680
One should be patient.

00:10:25.920 --> 00:10:31.540
When it's like now, with around minus 10 degrees celcius in Stockholm ...

00:10:31.540 --> 00:10:34.460
... do you sometimes regret the method you've chosen?

00:10:36.520 --> 00:10:40.500
Sometimes, maybe. When you have to ride a bike in minus ten degrees.

00:10:40.960 --> 00:10:44.320
Early in the morning. Then you might think that ...

00:10:44.660 --> 00:10:46.120
But, no.

00:10:46.120 --> 00:10:50.860
No, because you can see that i still makes a little bit of a difference, and ...

00:10:51.140 --> 00:10:57.760
You need to wear layers. Lots of layers. And you can bring tea. And you can jump!

00:11:03.000 --> 00:11:08.860
Greta, next week, you're heading to the ...

00:11:08.880 --> 00:11:11.580
... big economic forum in Davos.

00:11:12.120 --> 00:11:19.120
You're going to meet Bono, amongst others. And I know that John Kerry, the former Secretary of State to the US, has asked for you to come.

00:11:19.400 --> 00:11:23.940
And then you're going to Rome to speak in front of the Pope.

00:11:24.160 --> 00:11:26.000
When you travel to Davos ...

00:11:27.240 --> 00:11:33.240
That is a place where most people arrive in their private jets, at least quite a lot of them.

00:11:33.300 --> 00:11:35.060
How will you travel there?

00:11:36.260 --> 00:11:37.860
Train. The night train.

00:11:38.100 --> 00:11:41.840
In total, I think it will be 65 hours back and forth.

00:11:41.840 --> 00:11:46.340
But then you can make sure you have things to do on the train, like writing speeches and things like that.

00:11:50.440 --> 00:11:54.000
Good luck with that, I'm so happy to have you in the show tonight.

00:11:54.000 --> 00:11:56.580
We're going to welcome another guest. Thank you so much!

